      "notes": [
        "Verified the new unit tests against main's markdown-import.ts: 4 of the 8 new tests fail on the old code (heading in body, rule in body, id-in-body, Connections-titled plain note after an export); the other 4 seam tests pass on main and act as regression guards for the new cutting rules. Full web suite (166 tests), tsc, pass on HEAD.",
        "Checked the exporter (internal/httpapi/export_handlers.go:196-238) against the claims: it writes exactly one `# ` (space name above the banner), one `## ` per thought, every thought ends in a metadata line (id/type/source/color/canvas, optionally `- line:`), Connections/Lines of thinking end in a connection/line entry, and no rule is ever written — so the seam rule holds for real exports. Origin/status/relation values all fit the regexes used by closesExportSection.",
        "Edge-case regression (not blocking, narrow): web/src/lib/markdown-import.ts:309-312 — when the banner block is closed by a thematic break instead of a `## ` (only happens for an export of an EMPTY space, i.e. `# name\\n\\nExported from umm…\\n\\n---\\n\\n<plain file>`), flush() sets insideExport=true and the rule is not treated as a seam, so the appended plain file is read by the exporter's rules and its `# ` headings no longer cut: '# 노트 A / 가 / # 노트 B / 나' came back as one thought. main returns two thoughts here. Fix would be to clear insideExport when the general-rules rule branch flushes a banner block.",
        "Known limitation carried over (documented in code): a `## ` heading inside a thought's body still cuts the thought, since it is indistinguishable from the exporter's own cut. Also a body whose last line looks like `- id: \\`…\\`` is still absorbed into metadata (pre-existing behaviour of withoutExportMetadata).",
        "Scope: the commit bundles an unrelated e2e fix (web/e2e/canvas.spec.ts) with the importer change. It is justified as a CI fix for main and the change is sound (notes are posted before the space is opened so the per-space saved viewport does not capture a partial fit). Minor stale wording: the new comment says 'the reload below restored it' but the reload was removed in this same change.",
        "Not able to run the Playwright e2e locally in this session; relied on the commit's stated 4/4 local reproduction."
      ],
